hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1228","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb told me, my uncle, Amr, meaning Ibn al-Harith, informed me, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of al-Dahhak al-Qurashi, on the authority of Anas, and Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Bakr bin Mudar told us, Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Bukayr bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Abdullah Al-Qurashi, he narrated it, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace On a journey, he prayed eight rak’ahs of the morning prayer, and when he left, he said: “Indeed, I prayed a prayer of desire and fear, so I asked my Lord for three, and He gave me Two times, and he denied me one. I asked him not to kill my nation for years, and he did. I asked him not to make an enemy against them, and he did. I asked him not to He classifies them as sects, but he refused to me.” Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman said: “Not to afflict my nation with years.”"
